From a6110b07647c427835245241479fcf51563f4bf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Captain Polliwog build <build@captainpolliwog.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:49:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 49/53] JSC: PowerPC baseline JIT, work in progress

A new assembler and macro assembler (PPCAssemblerJIT.h,
MacroAssemblerPPCJIT.h) used only when ENABLE(JIT), plus the PowerPC paths
in CCallHelpers, AssemblyHelpers, the native call thunks and the frame
shuffler. Big-endian fixes: JSValue results come back tag first in r3, and
the callee and argument count header slots keep their payloads at +4. The
JIT is off unless the build enables it (the leopard-g4-jit variant); the
regular expression and CSS JITs keep using PPCAssembler.h.
